    "projects": [
      {
        "title": "PeaceTok",
        "start_date": "Mar 2026",
        "description": "Reverse engineered TikTok's internal rendering pipeline using runtime object inspection to intercept video models and comment cells before they ever hit the screen. By hooking directly into TikTok's For You page feed data source, the tweak surgically removes matched content from the render queue at the data layer. Since the hooks occur at the interpretation process, the app flow and UI remain untouched, meaning blocked content never touches the view hierarchy at all.Keyword matching runs across 10+ metadata fields per video (captions, hashtags, stickers, song name, author info), with a secondary playback guard hook as a fallback intercept. Ships with a native in-app preferences UI and a live session filter counter."
      }
